<div class="page" id="page-about">
  <div class="dark-hero"><div class="dark-hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--ci-crema-light)">Who we are</p>
    <h1>About Crema Italia</h1>
    <p>A Florida based importer and curator of specialty Italian coffee. Not a roaster.</p>
  </div></div>
  <main class="ci-main">
    <!-- PROD: copy below is provisional - Steve to provide final language for each tile. -->
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">Chi siamo</p><h2>Our company</h2></div>
    <div class="founder-grid" id="company-grid">
      <div class="founder-col">
        <img class="founder-photo" src="{{ 'ci-company.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A view of Tuscany" width="200" height="200" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <p class="person-role">Tuscany</p>
        <figure class="story-photo founder-stack">
          <img src="{{ 'ci-company-door.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A weathered caff&egrave; door in Sarteano, Tuscany" width="440" height="619" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <figcaption>A <span class="ita">caff&egrave;</span> door - Sarteano.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Crema Italia, LLC imports curated whole-bean coffee from a small, named group of artisan Italian roasters, stores it in our Florida warehouse, and ships it to American customers&hellip; unchanged. We bring their coffee to you just as if you were there, in Italy.</p>
        <p>We import; we never interfere. Each roaster&rsquo;s coffee reaches you exactly as they roast and seal it - nothing re-roasted, re-ground, or re-bagged. We are the U.S. Agent for FDA food-facility registration on behalf of our roaster partners.</p>
        <h3 id="company-3ps">The Three P&rsquo;s</h3>
        <div class="beats">
          <p><strong>Place.</strong> Espresso was born in Italy, and coffee lovers worldwide recognize Italian roasts as balanced, refined, and delicious.</p>
          <p><strong>Product.</strong> We import a carefully selected collection of roasted beans. Why beans? Because when you grind them fresh, you open a fresh bit of Italy in your cup.</p>
          <p><strong>People.</strong> From our team to our roasters to our customers, we are a group passionate about coffee - and the culture around it.</p>
        </div>
        <p>At the core, it&rsquo;s always about people. These three P&rsquo;s set our tone, define who we are, and shape our principles.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Il nostro fondatore</p><h2>Our founder</h2></div>
    <div class="founder-grid">
      <div class="founder-col">
        <img class="founder-photo" src="{{ 'ci-founder.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Steve Roberts, Founder" width="200" height="200" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <h4 class="founder-name">Steve Roberts</h4>
        <p class="person-role">Founder</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Steve Roberts is the founder of Crema Italia. His road to Italy is a long one - here is a brief recap, in his words:</p>
        <p>I am a dog person, but I&rsquo;ve lived a cat life. Meaning I&rsquo;m on life number six.</p>
        <div class="founder-lives">
          <p><strong>Life one.</strong> In pursuit of a professional music career as a French horn player - but my high C in Till Eulenspiegel was meek. Next.</p>
          <p><strong>Life two.</strong> I discovered computers, wrote a lot of custom software, and left the horn behind.</p>
          <p><strong>Life three.</strong> I founded a restaurant back-office company. It grew - and took me to Europe, then Italy, where I discovered espresso.</p>
          <p><strong>Life four.</strong> We sold the software business to a bigger one.</p>
          <p><strong>Life five.</strong> Retirement: family, kids, grandchildren, travel, mountain biking, flying airplanes, incredible new friends. Italy became my go-to place; Tuscany melts my heart (repeat, multiple times and counting).</p>
          <p><strong>Life six.</strong> <span class="ita">Allora</span> - the inspiration for Crema Italia. Two things in mind: bring amazing fresh coffee from amazing Italian roasters into the US, and help the people I love help me build it - so they can enjoy a few extra lives too.</p>
        </div>
        <p>Stay tuned - I&rsquo;ve a few lives remaining. Oh, did I say I start every morning with an espresso? I don&rsquo;t. I start with three.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

