<!-- ============================== FAQ ============================== -->
<div class="page" id="page-faq">
  <main class="ci-main">
    <button class="back-btn" onclick="goBack()">&larr; Back</button>
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>FAQ</h2></div>
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:72ch">
      <h3>Do you sell ground coffee?</h3>
      <p>No. Everything is whole bean, because that is what our roasters seal in valve bags at origin. Grind fresh just before you brew. If you do not have a grinder, search for a burr grinder in our <button class="inline-link" onclick="showPage('bottega')">Bottega</button>.</p>
      <h3>How fresh is the coffee, and which bag do I get?</h3>
      <p>We purchase the same coffee routinely which is why we sometimes quote a roast date range. We
      always fulfill orders in the order that we receive inventory, or First In First Out (FIFO), in
      inventory-speak. If a particular lot is out of our immediate freshness window, it is moved to our
      Offerta shelf and priced accordingly. We do not fulfill subscriptions with products that exceed
      our freshness promise on the date of shipping to you.</p>
      <p>In rare circumstances where an Offerta lot exceeds our freshness promise entirely, we endeavor
      to donate this coffee to worthy recipients. Remember, commercial coffee is typically sold as fresh
      within a 24-month freshness window.</p>
      <p>Please note that any order of more than one bag may span lots, but the freshness of spanned lots
      is always in the favor of the customer. We want you to enjoy fresh coffee.</p>
      <h3>Do you roast the coffee?</h3>
      <p>No. We import and curate; the roasters roast. We never roast, blend, or repackage.</p>
      <h3>How do subscriber discounts work?</h3>
      <p>An active Roccia subscription gives 10% off Roccia, Sorpresa, and Selezione (Founding Members - the first {{ settings.founding_member_cap }} subscribers at launch - receive 12% for life). Offerta and Bottega are never discounted. Discounts never stack: you always receive the single highest one you qualify for. A one-time first-purchase 5% applies only when it is your best rate, so a subscriber's first order still gets their 10%, or a Founding Member's 12%, whichever is higher, never both added together.</p>
      <h3>What goes in the discount code field at checkout?</h3>
      <p>Nothing. We do not issue promo/discount codes, to anyone, ever. No launch codes, no newsletter codes, no influencer codes. Any discount you have earned is calculated for you when you log in and check out.</p>
      <h3>How does gifting work?</h3>
      <p>Tick <strong>This order is a gift</strong> in your cart and add a short note. We print it on a card and put it in the box. Nothing inside any package we ship shows a price - gift or not - so there is nothing to remember and nothing to go wrong. Your receipt reaches you by email, never the box.</p>
      <p>Two things worth knowing. A gift ships to one address, so if you are buying for yourself and for someone else at the same time, place two orders. And <strong>subscriptions cannot be gifted</strong> - a subscription bills your card on its cadence and ships to a single address, so the gift option is not offered on any order that contains one. If you want to give someone coffee regularly, buy it for them as separate orders whenever you like.</p>
      <h3>How fresh is the coffee?</h3>
      <p>Best within {{ settings.freshness_window_days }} days of the roast date, which we always show. Sorpresa collections are assembled on-demand so every bag ships fresh.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>

